[gd_scene load_steps=8 format=3]

; Riftwrought — the ISOLATED ROGUELITE BUILD VARIETY V1 REVIEW (decision D-223).
;
; Nexus -> Rift Gate -> a SEEDED route of three authored rooms -> TWO seeded
; temporary-upgrade choices, one after the opening room and one after the reward
; room -> elite -> Nexus. Built to be PLAYED and judged: do temporary upgrade
; COMBINATIONS create meaningfully different play styles?
;
; IT IS NOT THE PROJECT ENTRYPOINT AND MUST NEVER BECOME ONE. `run/main_scene`
; is still `res://scenes/app/prototype_app.tscn`, and this scene is launched
; explicitly. It loads no other scene, writes nothing to disk, adds no InputMap
; action, and touches no accepted value.
;
; IT REPLACES NEITHER ACCEPTED REVIEW. `scenes/roguelite/roguelite_core_loop.tscn`
; (D-220/D-221) and `scenes/roguelite/roguelite_replayability_review.tscn`
; (D-222) are both preserved byte-identical, both still run, and both remain
; working baselines; their own runners still guard them and this review's runner
; runs both of their verifications once.
;
; IT ADDS NO ROOM AND NO ENEMY. The nine authored greybox rooms, the fifteen
; enemies, the three beats, the seeded route selection, the walk-in gates, the
; reward placement, the Nexus, the death path and every control are D-222's and
; D-220's, inherited and unedited. What this review adds is the temporary
; UPGRADE POOL, the second choice moment, and a brief on-ground outline of the
; swing that actually happened so the two spatial upgrades can be judged by eye.
;
; DELIBERATELY GREYBOXED, AND THE CLAIM IS SCOPED HONESTLY. Every surface, mass,
; gate, marker and outline THIS REVIEW draws is primitive Godot geometry in a
; flat material, built in code: no environment asset, texture, shader file,
; particle system or new third-party payload, and the review's own scripts name
; none. What it does NOT claim is that no registered asset is on screen — the
; reused, unmodified kernels bring their own already-registered models with them
; (the KayKit player and Graveblade rigs from Gate A, and the registered sword
; model Gate 1D's `FirstMvpItemDrop` shows for a ground item). That is reuse of
; an accepted, already-inventoried asset through an unedited class, not a new
; asset and not an art pass: the third-party inventory is asserted unchanged at
; 185 + 2 = 187.
;
; No Riftfall Landing or Broken Watch node exists in this scene — see
; `roguelite_build_variety_runtime.gd`'s header for why the runtime extends
; `RogueliteReplayabilityRuntime` (which extends `RogueliteCoreLoopRuntime`,
; which extends `BrokenWatchSlice` for its TYPE) and then deliberately does not
; call its `_ready()`.
;
; `FallenOverlay` is declared here as Gate 1D's own overlay and REPLACED at
; runtime by the accepted `RogueliteFallenOverlay`, exactly as both accepted
; reviews do, so the whole proven modal contract is inherited rather than copied.
;
; Controls are Gate 1D's, unchanged. Review keys are PHYSICAL:
;   F6 grid · F7 next seeded route (Nexus only) · F8 swing outline
;   [ ] camera distance · \ reset · F5 abandon the run
;
; Run it directly:
;   /Applications/Godot.app/Contents/MacOS/Godot --path game \
;     res://scenes/roguelite/roguelite_build_variety_review.tscn
;
; Enter a named run:
;   ... roguelite_build_variety_review.tscn -- --seed 12345

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/roguelite/build_variety/roguelite_build_variety_runtime.gd" id="1_runtime"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/prototype_zero/destination_marker.gd" id="2_marker"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/camera/prototype_camera_rig.gd" id="3_camera"]
